cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Equity-Weighted Physician Allocation Across New Jersey
  Emergency Departments
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rithvik
    family-names: Sharma
abstract: >-
  An M/M/c queueing model of New Jersey emergency departments with an
  inverse solver that recovers each hospital's implied physician capacity
  from observed CMS wait times, and an equity-weighted greedy allocation
  algorithm that distributes additional physician capacity across the
  network while accounting for county-level CDC Social Vulnerability Index
  scores.
keywords:
  - operations research
  - queueing theory
  - health equity
  - emergency department
  - resource allocation
license: MIT
